# eventsintel runtime config template.
# Copy to a private location and export before running. Do NOT commit real values.
# The normal binary reads EVENTSINTEL_* env vars (config.FromEnv); the separate
# eventscout-server also reads EVENTSCOUT_TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS; there is no config file.

# --- Core (see internal/config/config.go for full list + defaults) ---
# EVENTSINTEL_HTTP_ADDR=:8080
# EVENTSINTEL_DB_PATH=eventsintel.db
# EVENTSINTEL_USER_AGENT="eventsintel/1.0 (+https://events.nukk.net)"

# --- Cloudflare cache purge (ingest unit only; optional) ---
# EVENTSINTEL_CF_PURGE_ZONE=
# EVENTSINTEL_CF_PURGE_TOKEN=        # secret

# --- Solar agent (ingest/agent commands; never on normal read path) ---
# Upstage Solar is OpenAI-compatible. Get an operator key at
# https://console.upstage.ai. This is a server-operator secret: never expose it
# to eventscout-server callers, never place it in a goal, and never commit/log it.
# The isolated `eventscout-server` refuses to start without this key, even when a
# local backend is configured. The eventscout CLI can use its local backend
# without Solar; pass `-backend solar` only when this key is intentionally set.
# EVENTSINTEL_SOLAR_API_KEY=         # operator secret — do NOT commit
# EVENTSINTEL_SOLAR_BASE_URL=https://api.upstage.ai/v1
# EVENTSINTEL_SOLAR_MODEL=solar-open2

# --- eventscout provider selection ---
# `go run ./cmd/eventscout` defaults to the keyless `public` provider (a bounded,
# server-owned seed catalog). `fixture` is explicit offline mode, not the default.
# `tavily` is explicit third-party mode and requires the key below; public mode
# does not read this variable.

# --- Tavily web search (eventscout -search-provider tavily; optional) ---
# Create a key at https://app.tavily.com and keep the real value only in an
# ignored local .env file or the process environment. Never commit or log it.
# EVENTSINTEL_TAVILY_API_KEY=        # secret — do NOT commit

# --- Anonymous eventscout-server (optional separate binary) ---
# It reads EVENTSCOUT_HTTP_ADDR and defaults to 127.0.0.1:8081 when this binary
# starts (the normal eventsintel API has its own :8080 default in config).
# EVENTSCOUT_HTTP_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8081
# Optional comma-separated proxy CIDRs. Only trusted proxy peers may supply the
# first valid X-Forwarded-For address for anonymous quota identity.
# EVENTSCOUT_TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=

# --- Local A/B model (optional; compare Korean extraction vs Solar) ---
# EVENTSINTEL_LOCAL_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:18900/v1
# EVENTSINTEL_LOCAL_MODEL=qwen36-dwq
